Features
A huge cast of different enemies and bosses;
All of which can be killed faster than it takes you to pass gas.
Tons of different equipment upgrades;
Which are all cosmetic.
Includes Idle elements where your miners collect gold while you are away from the game;
A feature that is so pointless I forgot it was there. It takes 10 seconds to max out your gold in one stage so I'm not sure why you would need a miner to gather 10 gold an hour.
Lovingly crafted Retro graphics;
So when you're running at 100+ speed it will look like a giant blur.
Achievements to unlock;
20 total. It takes 5 minutes to unlock 19 and hours to unlock the last.
Bestiary to fill out;
Another pointless feature. This is like having a checklist for your Chess game.
Cards to collect;
Only good thing about this game. You can sell the cards so you don't feel entirely cheated.
Controller support;
YES, the "Right" direction works. I never tried any other button since this is all you need.
Possibly infinite gameplay;
They use the word "Possibly" because all people who have tried to reach the end killed themselves before that point.
Ridiculous amounts of Loot and XP!
By "loot" they mean "gold" because there is nothing else to collect. As for XP, I'm not sure why it's even there. You can gain levels but it has no impact on the game since everything scales with the upgrades you buy.
My final note: I almost fell asleep while playing this. Not even worth $0.50 since you wont make that back from card sales.
